   156	## 5. Positive-branch logic for the M0 classification
   157	
   158	A three-arm study must be able to resolve **both** branches. A design powered
   159	only for branch L is insufficient (Draft v3 section 6.3). Therefore:
   160	
   161	- **NOT FEASIBLE** follows when a necessary condition of **either** branch is
   162	  shown unattainable by the method-independent bound in section 7.4.
   163	- **FEASIBLE AS PROPOSED** would require branch-level power >= 0.80 for both
   164	  branches under the least-favorable registered alternatives. Under v1 it is
   165	  unreachable in the public-proxy domain (section 7.3).
