   167	## 6. Supply bounds and missingness
   168	
   169	### 6.1 Supply bounds (from R2B, within the frozen frame)
   170	
   171	R2B reports, for the frozen frame:
   172	
   173	| Quantity | Definition |
   174	|---|---|
   175	| `H_conf` | Historical clusters confirmed eligible under the frozen R3 rules, with complete provenance |
   176	| `H_unres` | Enumerated items whose eligibility is missing or indeterminate (including extraction failures for enumerated items) |
   177	| `H_enum_max` | A certified upper bound on the number of items in the frame that could form clusters, taken from a complete enumeration (for example a platform-reported total count for the window) that the frozen extraction specification names in advance. If no certified enumeration exists for any repository in the frame, `H_enum_max` is **unbounded**. |
   178	| `H_high` | `min(H_conf + H_unres + (H_enum_max - enumerated items), H_enum_max)`, that is, every item that is not confirmed ineligible for a recorded, rule-based reason is counted as potentially eligible; unbounded if `H_enum_max` is unbounded |
   179	| `F_high` | `floor(H_high / 0.75)`: the largest final pool permitted when the pilot reservation is zero and authored clusters fill the maximum 25% weight. Authored supply is neither invented beyond that cap nor set to zero. |
   180	
   181	Clusters excluded for a recorded rule-based cause are excluded from all bounds.
   182	Missing eligibility is never counted as ineligible (that would fabricate
   183	scarcity). Historical and forward supply are reported separately; forward
   184	supply cannot substitute for G0.
   185	
   186	### 6.2 Missingness, invalid runs, and invalid epochs
   187	
   188	| Situation | Frozen treatment |
   189	|---|---|
   190	| Gate NOT MEASURABLE IN DOMAIN | Recorded as missing for that gate; never treated as passed, failed, zero, or "not applicable" |
   191	| Unbounded or uncertified `H_enum_max` | The supply route to NOT FEASIBLE is disabled |
   192	| R2B extraction run or R4 run with a pin/hash mismatch, a frozen-rule violation, an input registered after outputs were seen, or an unrecorded configuration change | **Invalid run.** Retained in the manifest with reason; not used. One rerun from the identical pre-declared specification is permitted. The first valid run binds; choosing among valid runs is prohibited. |
   193	| Upstream gate EXPIRED, REVOKED, or INVALIDATED (#1370 lifecycle rules) | Every dependent output is invalid from that time; the classification is UNADJUDICATED |
   194	| Future study (modeled by R4): failed, crashed, refused, exhausted, or unreviewed slot | Failed slot carrying its full cost; never removed from any denominator |
   195	| Future study: held-out correctness or severity evaluation missing for an **accepted** artifact | Acceptance and cost records are kept. For the bound on each component, the missing outcome is imputed adversarially to the claim: in the subject arm, not correct and serious escape; in the comparator arm, correct and no escape. If such imputations exceed 5% of accepted slots in any arm, the epoch is INVALID. |
   196	| Future study: protocol or trust defect | Epoch INVALID; affected evidence identified; no favorable old runs retained (Draft v3 section 6.4) |
   197	
   198	## 7. Classification rules

