The applicability check found a counterexample: a frozen criticality mix can permit a valid safety test with 80.17% power at 161 clusters, below the new cutoff of 174. The contamination proof is valid for its unrestricted model, but the rules have not shown that model covers every design the original M0 rules permit. I also found a remaining gap in R0 dependency binding and an undefined route state for invalid measurements.
